;; manifest/bot-allowances.edn — what each itonami bot may spend, and on which rail.
;;
;; THIS FILE IS THE ISSUANCE POLICY, NOT THE AUTHORITY.
;;
;; It says what the operator has decided to GRANT. What a bot carries is a
;; Biscuit minted from it by `scripts/x402_bot_pass.cljs`, and what the payer
;; trusts is the verified grant inside that token — folded by
;; `biscuit.kotoba/->delegated`, decided by `kotoba-lang/authority`.
;;
;; Until 2026-08-31 this file WAS the authority: an unsigned EDN that only the
;; payer read. Under this workspace's own division that is a delegation, and
;; delegation is a Biscuit (ADR-2608291700: "CACAO は session の起点として残り
;; delegation からは降りている"; ADR-2608312900-hyakka: "支払いは authorization
;; ではない。x402 が決済し、biscuit が『その支払いが何を買ったか』を運び、
;; authority が決める"). Being named here is now necessary and NOT sufficient:
;; a bot with no pass is refused with `:pass/absent` before a socket opens.
;;
;; DENY BY DEFAULT is unchanged. A bot that has not been told what it may spend
;; has not been authorised to spend anything, and the most dangerous default
;; here is the one that reads silence as freedom (kotoba-lang/pay
;; `x402-buyer`: "no policy is not permission").
;;
;; WHY CREDITS AND NOT USDC. The only rail an unattended process can settle
;; without holding money is murakumo credits: labour-issued, transferable
;; between holders, NON-redeemable for fiat/USDC/EN by design (ADR-2607995000
;; §1). A bot paying in credits is spending an allowance inside this economy,
;; not moving funds. The USDC rail stays available to a HUMAN or an operator
;; who chooses it; no bot is granted it here, and a bot cannot grant itself one
;; because this file is the policy and the bot does not write it.
;;
;; UNITS ARE PER RAIL. `:credits/per-call` is credits, not micro-USDC. The two
;; arrive as the same string in the same field of the same 402 challenge, so
;; the cap is keyed by rail on the way into the buyer policy.
;;
;; A COMMITTED ALLOWANCE IS NOT A FUNDED ONE, AND AN ISSUED PASS IS NOT AN
;; ENFORCED ONE. Naming a bot here permits a spend; it does not create a
;; balance, and today the payer is still the only party that reads the pass —
;; seller-side enforcement needs the ledger to accept it, which is murakumo's
;; decision. An unfunded bot is refused by the
;; ledger with `insufficient-credits`, which is the correct answer and a
;; different one from "not allowed".

{:allowance/version 1

 ;; The credits ledger of record. Balances are read from `<ledger>/infer/credits`
 ;; and transfers are appended by the FACILITATOR, not by the bot: the bot mints
 ;; a CACAO naming one (recipient, amount) and hands it over, which is the
 ;; difference between paying someone and giving them your account.
 :allowance/ledger "https://api.murakumo.cloud"

 ;; Sellers a bot may pay at all, by their credits account name. A name and not
 ;; an address: credits have no chain.
 :allowance/sellers #{"murakumo" "kotobase"}

 ;; The rail every allowance below is denominated in, in preference order.
 ;; `pay.x402-buyer` refuses to CHOOSE between rails whose amounts are not
 ;; comparable, so this is what makes a two-offer challenge decidable.
 :allowance/rails [["murakumo" "CREDITS"]]

 ;; Every id says WHERE it is anchored, so the name can be checked against
 ;; something rather than taken on trust. `scripts/verify-bot-allowances.cljs`
 ;; resolves each one and REFUSES to report a clean registry when it could not
 ;; ask — an id nothing answers to is dead policy, and a real bot missing from
 ;; this file silently cannot pay.
 ;;
 ;;   :runs-as/launchd  — a plist in ~/Library/LaunchAgents (this host)
 ;;   :runs-as/skill    — a skill in .claude/skills (invoked by a loop or by hand)
 ;;   :runs-as/hermes   — a Hermes cron job; its jobs live in Hermes's own
 ;;                       SQLite, so this one cannot be checked from the tree
 ;;                       and is reported UNVERIFIED rather than ok
 :allowance/bots
 {"repo-bot-drain"
  {:credits/per-call 1 :credits/per-day 20
   :runs-as/launchd "cloud.itonami.bot.repo-bot-drain" :runs-as/skill "repo-bot-drain"}

  "docs-edn-repair"
  {:credits/per-call 1 :credits/per-day 10 :runs-as/skill "docs-edn-repair"}

  "adr-inventory"
  {:credits/per-call 1 :credits/per-day 10 :runs-as/skill "adr-inventory"}

  "rule-kaizen"
  {:credits/per-call 1 :credits/per-day 10 :runs-as/skill "rule-kaizen"}

  "itonami-ingest-scout"
  {:credits/per-call 1 :credits/per-day 30 :runs-as/hermes "itonami-ingest-scout"}

  "itonami-coverage-scout"
  {:credits/per-call 1 :credits/per-day 30 :runs-as/hermes "itonami-coverage-scout"}

  ;; amu の速度主張チェーン。measurement placement を直して host gate を開け、
  ;; qualified な bounded claim を着地させる（ADR 0341）。plan は
  ;; .hermes/plans/2026-09-07_092400-amu-claim-chain.md、hermes job 52c20791b602。
  ;; per-day が 20min cron の 72 回より小さいのは意図的 —— 測れない tick は
  ;; 何も呼ばずに "not measured" で終わるのが正しい挙動なので、上限は
  ;; 「実際に測れた回数」の想定に合わせてある。
  "amu-claim-chain"
  {:credits/per-call 1 :credits/per-day 40 :runs-as/hermes "amu-claim-chain"}}}
